	(uuid "5de2cbf4-e06d-593f-a0fb-77a0c6d93132")
	(paper "A2")
	(title_block
		(title "PATIENT: main ECG + pad-impedance front end ADS1292R (64 kHz respiration carrier) with defibrillation protection")
		(date "2026-11-27")
		(rev "A-draft")
		(company "Open AED project — CERN-OHL-S-2.0 — NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION")
		(comment 1 "NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION — unreviewed design")
		(comment 2 "Source: docs/HARDWARE_DESIGN.md v0.3 §B3; hardware/aed-main/contract.md issue 3 §5.8, §8, §10; rev3-changes.md WP-H H-4; capture notes WP-H")
		(comment 3 "Every tap: patient side = defibrillator-rated DPCR resistor (+ 2 x 3 kV C0G on drive taps) -> TVS to GND -> inner resistor -> chip pin.")
		(comment 4 "Excitation is limited by the ADS1292R itself (100 uA max): ~80 uA here, NOT the 0.34 mA the design assumed (notes).")
		(comment 5 "Revision 0.3 (H-4, D-67): the ECG branch has its own 51 k DPCR sense resistors R1528/R1529 and clamps D1506/D1507, so the ECG filter C1505 no longer shunts the 64 kHz impedance signal.")
		(comment 6 "Generated by tools/schgen from the sheet spec — edit the spec, not this file (until schematic freeze)")
	)
