	(text_box "Drive taps (respiration excitation RESP_MODP -> pad A, RESP_MODN -> pad B): 2 x 4.7 nF 3 kV C0G + 2 x 24 k DPCR in parallel + TVS + 2.0 k"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 269.385 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2f6d0ead-d21d-5e2e-a376-2760c840559c")
	)
	(text_box "Excitation: the ADS1292R modulator is a square wave of amplitude VREFP (2.42 V) with a datasheet MAXIMUM of 100 uA (SBAS502C EC p.8); current = 2.42 V / loop impedance. Loop = 2 x (12 k + 2.0 k) + 2 x 1.06 k (2.35 nF at 64 kHz) + pads <=\n0.25 k = 30.4 k -> ~80 uA [CALC]. The design's '1 k drive resistor, 0.34 mA' is impossible with this chip (contract issue).\nWhy DPCR 24 k x 2 in parallel instead of the contract's 1 k pulse resistor: an external 5 kV defibrillator pulse puts up to ~5 kV across this resistor before the 2.35 nF charges (tau = 12 k x 2.35 nF = 28 us); no 1 k part found is rated\nabove ~1.75 kV (Vishay CRCW2512-HP Umax), while TT DPCR is tested with 100 pulses of 5 kV peak (IEC 60601-2-27). DPCR's range starts at 20 k, so two 24 k (E24) in parallel give 12 k. Each sees <= 5 kV, ~15 mJ per external pulse (1/2 C V^2\nsplit) [CALC].\nCapacitors (two in series per pad, so one shorted capacitor still blocks DC): C0G 4.7 nF 3 kV exists only in 3640 (Knowles AEC-Q200 range; Vishay/KEMET max 3.3-4 nF) [MPN derived from the ordering code: verify]. Voltage per capacitor: own\nshock 2,182 V -> <= 1.1 kV; external 5 kV -> ~1.25 kV balanced, <= 2.5 kV one-sided.\nTVS D1501/D1502 Bourns CDSOD323-T03C (bidirectional, VWM 3.3 V, VBR >= 4.0 V, 350 W 8/20 us, 3 pF, 5 uA): takes the edge current (<= 5 kV / 12 k = 0.42 A, tau 28 us). It CANNOT clamp below the chip's 3.6 V abs max (no 3.3 V TVS has VBR <\n4 V): the 2.0 k inner resistor limits the pin current to <= (6.5 - 3.6) / 2 k = 1.5 mA, inside the chip's +/-10 mA continuous rating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 269.385 21.431)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "82f56fe6-d85c-5730-b9d3-afebadacbfc0")
	)
	(text_box "Sense taps, two per pad: impedance R1507/R1508 51 k DPCR + TVS + 10 k + 2.2 nF (IN1); ECG R1528/R1529 51 k DPCR + TVS + 10 k (IN2)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 123.061 0)
		(size 268.95 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5ad1bf5d-7450-5fce-a77c-a3c268fe54a6")
	)
	(text_box "External 5 kV pulse: <= 98 mA one-sided (49 mA balanced) through each 51 k; <= 0.74 J one-sided per pulse (V^2 tau / 2R with tau = 3.4 ms); DPCR rating = 100 pulses of 5 kV peak, single-pulse curve ~1.5 kW at 1 ms. Own shock 2,182 V for\nup to 20 ms (relay fault): 43 mA, 93 W, 1.9 J per resistor; curve ~250 W at 20 ms [CALC; curve values read from the graph].\nTVS currents 43-98 mA for milliseconds: energy small (<= 5 mJ) but outside the 8/20 us rating basis [UNVERIFIED for ms pulses]. Chip pin current through 10 k <= 0.34 mA.\nECG (channel 2): IN2P/IN2N DC-coupled through 61 k per side; C1505 470 pF C0G differential: 2.8 kHz pole against the charger's 3-43 kHz band [CALC]. IN2 common mode set by the RLD amplifier (below).\nRespiration (channel 1): R1507/R1508 -> clamp D1503/D1504 (PT_MSA_CL/PT_MSB_CL) -> 10 k + 2.2 nF C0G into IN1P/IN1N, biased at mid-supply by 10 M to AVDD and 10 M to GND each (datasheet Figure 68 arrangement).\nRevision 0.3 (H-4): in issue 2 the ECG resistors R1509/R1510 hung on the same clamp nodes, so C1505 (5.3 k at 64 kHz) shunted ~85 % of the impedance signal (simulated 25-34 mohm RMS against < 10 mohm, LR §6). Now the ECG branch has its\nown R1528/R1529 51 k DPCR from PT_FE_A/PT_FE_B to new clamp nodes PT_ESA_CL/PT_ESB_CL with D1506/D1507 (same parts as R1507/D1503). Simulated (sim/rev3-wph/imp_ecg_noise_wph.cir): IN1 sees 0.97 of the pad voltage (was 0.17); impedance\nnoise 4.6-6.3 mohm RMS (chip noise 0.13 uV/rtHz EST). ECG gain 0.99 and ECG resistor noise 0.28 uV RMS (0.5-40 Hz) unchanged.\nProtection per tap unchanged (each new resistor/TVS sees what R1507/D1503 see: 5 kV external pulse one-sided 97 mA, 0.83 J; own shock bound 2,409 V for 19.9 ms 47 mA, 2.26 J) [SIM rev3-wph fe_protect_wph.cir]. Resistive sense taps per pad\nrise from 2 x 51 k (R1507 + the supervisor's R1605) to 3 x 51 k, so pad to pad 51 k -> 34 k: diverts ~0.3 % (was ~0.2 %) of an external defibrillator's energy into a 100 ohm patient [CALC].\nNo test points (R9)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 129.411 0)
		(size 268.95 25.749)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3cd47378-680f-5470-b119-b3baae1a155d")
	)
	(text_box "Bias with two electrodes: RLD amplifier as mid-supply driver into both ECG inputs through 10 M"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 315.105 25.4 0)
		(size 162.92 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8dea8f40-795c-5772-b058-37a3efffd4fe")
	)
	(text_box "No third (right-leg) electrode exists. With RESP2.RLDREF_INT = 1 the RLD amplifier references (AVDD+AVSS)/2; RLDOUT drives each ECG input node\nthrough 10 M (R1513, R1514), which sets the patient's DC potential (the drive taps are DC-blocked, so this is the only DC path). Feedback R1527\n1 M || C1507 1.5 nF (datasheet typical). RLDIN/RLDREF tied to AVDD (datasheet: 'connect to AVDD if not used'). Whether to also sense the IN2\ncommon mode (RLD_SENS) is a firmware choice [the datasheet gives no explicit two-electrode guidance: UNVERIFIED].\nDC patient current from this path: both pads at the same potential -> ~0; with a 300 mV electrode offset <= 15 nA [CALC]."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 315.105 31.75 0)
		(size 162.92 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "13554885-e237-5c9d-9616-d65f55ca9c16")
	)
	(text_box "U1501 ADS1292R: channel 1 = impedance (respiration, internal clock, 64 kHz, RESP_CTRL = 0), channel 2 = ECG 250/s"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 315.105 80.105 0)
		(size 244.895 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "896877da-a5c0-5ecd-82e4-bbb32a2838c4")
	)
	(text_box "Clock: CLKSEL = 1 (internal 512 kHz, +/-1.5 % over -40..+85 C); CLK 3-stated (CLK_EN = 0), held by 100 k. 64 kHz respiration needs RESP_CTRL = 0 (internal clock mode) and RESP2.RESP_FREQ = 1. Recommended at 64 kHz:\nchannel 1 gain 2 or 3, phase 135-157.5 deg (SBAS502C p.63).\nReference: internal 2.42 V (CONFIG2.PDB_REFBUF = 1 required: power-up default is external), VREFP 10 uF || 0.1 uF; VREFN = AVSS. VCAP1, VCAP2 1 uF (datasheet: C0G/tantalum if the board vibrates — belt-worn, CPR: X7R\nused here, flagged).\nPGA filters: 47 nF across PGA1P/N (respiration; three datasheet places say 47 nF, one says 4.7 nF: flagged), 4.7 nF across PGA2P/N.\nGPIO1/2 unused: to GND through 10 k (datasheet). Supplies: AVDD_AFE from 3V3_MAIN via ferrite, 10 u + 1 u + 0.1 u; DVDD 3V3_MAIN 1 u + 0.1 u. AVDD shunt clamp D1505 ESD5Z3.3 (VBR >= 5.0 V, below the 5.5 V abs max):\nbackup only; the real limit on injected current is the inner resistors (<= ~4 mA total, absorbed by 3V3_MAIN's load) [notes].\nContract defaults: AFE_CS_N 100 k up, AFE_START 100 k down, AFE_RESET_N 100 k down (held in reset until the main controller releases it)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 315.105 86.455 0)
		(size 244.895 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7c0d1498-d41d-5c1f-84db-de85aa17f25f")
	)
